An exam is the container results are entered against. Create it before anyone starts marking.

## Steps

1. Open **Exams** in the side drawer.
2. Select **New Exam**.
3. Fill in:
   - **Exam Name** — what everyone will see in dropdowns and on reports. Include the year if you run
     the same exam annually (`Term 1 2026`, not `Term 1`).
   - **Exam Type** — one of **TERM**, **MIDTERM** or **SPECIAL**. This is not cosmetic:
     [progress reports](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-progress-reports) and term rankings are built from
     TERM exams, so a term exam typed as SPECIAL will not appear where you expect it.
   - **Date** — via **Pick Date**.
4. Select **Save**.

The exam now appears on the Exams dashboard, and classes can be opened under it.

## What to do next

- [Enter results](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-enter-exam-results), class by class and subject by
  subject — or [upload them from a spreadsheet](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-upload-exam-results).
- Check **Exams → Rankings** once enough subjects are in.
- Review any **Exams → Result Changes** raised against marks that are already saved.

